          The test-case database holds NO objective and NO step text for this case.  The
          objective and the 8 steps below were written down BEFORE the run, from three
          sources: the case title; the x960 Test Plan Specification (TPS) row 263
          "NTP / IPv6 NTP Client", Supported = Yes; and the DUT's own CLI surface, read
          read-only.  Each STEP heading below quotes the step text as it was designed.
          Objective as designed: "prove that the AT-x960-56YSQ acts as an NTP client over
          IPv6.  It must send IPv6 NTP mode-3 requests on the wire to a configured IPv6
          server.  It must be answered and reach synchronisation.  It must NOT use an
          IPv6 server that answers nothing.  It must correct a real clock error through
          the IPv6 association.  It must stop when the configuration is removed.  The
          configuration must survive a cold boot with nothing typed into the device."
