  => STEP 5 PASS: 170 s of capture, ZERO NTP packets.  The DUT's poll interval just
     before the removal was 64 s, so this window covers about 2.6 polls that would have
     happened and did not.  The same link carried 4 of 4 ICMPv6 echo replies at 0.5 ms in
     the middle of that same window, so the silence belongs to the DUT and not to a dead
     link.  The client stops completely when the configuration is removed.  No polling is
     left over.
     This capture's filter was `udp port 123` only, which is why the frame count is 0
     rather than "some ICMPv6 and no NTP".  The separate proof that the link was alive is
     the ping, taken on the same link at the same time.

